# haiku-repo-coherence.baseline -- EXACT (`==`) requirements that the live green
# pool already cannot satisfy (issue 708).
#
# These are pre-existing debt, not accepted design. Each line is a package that
# is UNINSTALLABLE right now. They are listed so that the coherence gate blocks
# NEW incoherence without blocking every unrelated publish; clearing one means
# rebuilding and republishing the port, after which `--strict-baseline` reports
# the line as STALE and it must be deleted. The list only shrinks.
#
# Format:  <pinning-package> <required-resolvable> <required-version>   # reason
# (the key is the first three fields; everything after `#` is the reason)
#
# Measured against s3://<pool>/debeos-repo-green/arm64/repo of 2026-10-14.

# --- base superseded out from under a subpackage (the issue-708 defect) ------
# haiku-repo-add's per-NAME supersede dropped the pinned base version; the
# subpackage is a different name, so the glob left it behind. Fix: rebuild and
# republish the subpackage at the base's current version.
ripgrep_debuginfo ripgrep 14.0.1      # base at 15.2.0-1; debuginfo never rebuilt

# --- base never published for arm64 at all -----------------------------------
# The arch-independent subpackage was published while its arch-specific base
# was not, so there is nothing to pin to. Fix: build the base for arm64, or drop
# the orphaned subpackage from the pool.
moleinvasion_music moleinvasion 0.4   # no moleinvasion-* in the arm64 pool

# --- resolvable never packaged for arm64 -------------------------------------
# No Java runtime is ported to Haiku arm64, so nothing can provide java:runtime.
# geogebra is unusable on this arch regardless of the repo's coherence.
geogebra java:runtime 8               # no JRE port for arm64
